At the same time, there are meaningful liabilities. A phenothiazine group is present (1), and that scaffold can be associated with less favorable oral exposure. The molecule has no acidic site, so the strongest acidic pKa is not defined, which removes one potential ionizable handle but does not by itself guarantee good exposure. The secondary hydroxyl is absent (0), which avoids an extra hydrogen-bond donor liability, but overall the structure still carries a tradeoff between a favorable low-polarity profile and the phenothiazine-related structural concern.

Balancing these factors, the very low TPSA, high QED, low-charge profile, and small neutral fraction outweigh the negative structural signal, so the molecule is more consistent with oral bioavailability at or above 20%."}

